### Example of Vulnerable Code

Here is an example of vulnerable code:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

void vulnerable_function(const char *format) {
    printf(format);
}

int main() {
    char user_input[100];
    printf("Enter a string: ");
    fgets(user_input, sizeof(user_input), stdin);

    // This is vulnerable to format string attacks
    vulnerable_function(user_input);

    return 0;
}
```

In this code, the `vulnerable_function` takes a format string directly from user input and passes it to `printf`. An attacker could input a string like `"%x %x %x %x"` to read the contents of the stack, or even more dangerous strings to write to arbitrary memory locations.

